      "x": 1129.2203366338654,
      "y": 1147.3621477674417,
      "width": 335.1197509765625,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1132748404,
      "version": 1085,
      "versionNonce": 1722243404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760080937646,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Video is served to frontend in\nbuffers using http range requests.\n2. No Preprocessing required as it\ncan only serve 1 type of file from\nbeginning to end.\n3. Doesn't dynamically adapt to \nnetwork conditions.\n4. Uses fix buffer size which \ndoesn't adapt to video quality\ni.e. Same 100KB buffer will be \nused regardless of quality of a \nvideo. In other words, a high \nquality  10s video is of 100MB \nand low quality 10s video is \nof 10 MB, both will use 100KB\nbuffer and thus doesn't scale for\nquality systems.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Video is served to frontend in\nbuffers using http range requests.\n2. No Preprocessing required as it\ncan only serve 1 type of file from\nbeginning to end.\n3. Doesn't dynamically adapt to \nnetwork conditions.\n4. Uses fix buffer size which \ndoesn't adapt to video quality\ni.e. Same 100KB buffer will be \nused regardless of quality of a \nvideo. In other words, a high \nquality  10s video is of 100MB \nand low quality 10s video is \nof 10 MB, both will use 100KB\nbuffer and thus doesn't scale for\nquality systems.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2Nys1THxcF40n5-XfQeLL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1483.0332211159962,
      "y": 1153.2619771068953,
      "width": 389.63970947265625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2106642252,
      "version": 967,
      "versionNonce": 1518440308,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760076911805,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Video is served in chunks usually\nof 1-2 seconds each\n2. Preprocess the video -- Divide in\nchunk, convert them to different video\nformates (.mp4, .avi, etc.), convert to\ndifferent codecs, can support multiple\nbit rates (1024P, 720P, 280P, etc).\n3. Dynamically adapt to network \nconditions (bandwidth, congestion, etc.)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Video is served in chunks usually\nof 1-2 seconds each\n2. Preprocess the video -- Divide in\nchunk, convert them to different video\nformates (.mp4, .avi, etc.), convert to\ndifferent codecs, can support multiple\nbit rates (1024P, 720P, 280P, etc).\n3. Dynamically adapt to network \nconditions (bandwidth, congestion, etc.)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
