      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "7bPS4vmiFp0R87fEATo7s",
      "originalText": "update\nmetadata",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "j2UWluMi81lmFRDJ0zlhq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1025.4847031306192,
      "y": 3614.1024333099085,
      "width": 922.4393310546875,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 541361868,
      "version": 2102,
      "versionNonce": 860658764,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760217257410,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Will implement option-1 but in production scenario likely option-2 or option-3 is better.\nAnother reason for option-1 is, we don't want to have static chunks. We want to chunk\nvideo based on frames (1-2 second) instead of bytes.\n\nAlso, there are few ways to get upload notification:\n1. Attach event listener using listenBucketNotification to a bucket. It allows monitoring\nlist of specific S3 events. A Listener method/function is attached to read notification\nand perform actions. It is pull-based notification mechanism that maintains a persistent \nconnection with the minIo server to constantly monitor for any changes. Ideal for real-time,\ntightly coupled monitoring but requires additional logic when connection fails.\n2. HTTP hooks/Message queues/Serverless functions like lambda. Define server endpoint \nto get http post notification when specific event occurs on a bucket. Similar to above \ncan monitor multiple events and take action one the notification http hook receives a \nnotification. The hook is configured using `mc admin` commands. It is push-based notification\nmechanism that relies on minIo to send notification for any change. Ideal for service oriented\narchitecture where systems are independent. Upon failure, consumer can read the messages\nfrom queue and process them.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Will implement option-1 but in production scenario likely option-2 or option-3 is better.\nAnother reason for option-1 is, we don't want to have static chunks. We want to chunk\nvideo based on frames (1-2 second) instead of bytes.\n\nAlso, there are few ways to get upload notification:\n1. Attach event listener using listenBucketNotification to a bucket. It allows monitoring\nlist of specific S3 events. A Listener method/function is attached to read notification\nand perform actions. It is pull-based notification mechanism that maintains a persistent \nconnection with the minIo server to constantly monitor for any changes. Ideal for real-time,\ntightly coupled monitoring but requires additional logic when connection fails.\n2. HTTP hooks/Message queues/Serverless functions like lambda. Define server endpoint \nto get http post notification when specific event occurs on a bucket. Similar to above \ncan monitor multiple events and take action one the notification http hook receives a \nnotification. The hook is configured using `mc admin` commands. It is push-based notification\nmechanism that relies on minIo to send notification for any change. Ideal for service oriented\narchitecture where systems are independent. Upon failure, consumer can read the messages\nfrom queue and process them.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
