      "text": "Store Chunks\n(Fragmented MP4s)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "9Lh1Q-ueQXTLP65NDgi_p",
      "originalText": "Store Chunks\n(Fragmented MP4s)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ape7EeA_A8vsaEL3d-ngJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1715.5274967761886,
      "y": 4796.785350292487,
      "width": 757.659423828125,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1746745922,
      "version": 920,
      "versionNonce": 1588753375,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762572845461,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can use JavaCV which is wrapper library for ffmpeg that can be used\nfor encoding, decoding and re-muxing files. Using FFmpegFrameGrabber, we\ncan grab frames and using FFmpegFrameRecoder we can write frames to a\nfile. Its important to make sure that proper headers are set in each chunk\nto be able to append to sourceBuffers on frontend MSE (otherwise video\nwill not play).\n\nSpecific to MP4. Using above method, we can split MP4s and using the proper\nmovflags in JavaCV (i.e. frag_keyframe+empty_moov+default_base_moof) we \ncan generate fragmented MP4s (a.k.a fmp4).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can use JavaCV which is wrapper library for ffmpeg that can be used\nfor encoding, decoding and re-muxing files. Using FFmpegFrameGrabber, we\ncan grab frames and using FFmpegFrameRecoder we can write frames to a\nfile. Its important to make sure that proper headers are set in each chunk\nto be able to append to sourceBuffers on frontend MSE (otherwise video\nwill not play).\n\nSpecific to MP4. Using above method, we can split MP4s and using the proper\nmovflags in JavaCV (i.e. frag_keyframe+empty_moov+default_base_moof) we \ncan generate fragmented MP4s (a.k.a fmp4).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
